    "section": "1. Method & Setup",
    "part": "Numerology Knowledge Base — Chaldean System",
    "text": "- Use the Chaldean letter map: 1 = A/I/J/Q/Y, 2 = B/K/R, 3 = C/G/L/S, 4 = D/M/T, 5 = E/H/N/X, 6 = U/V/W, 7 = O/Z, 8 = F/P. The digit 9 is sacred and is not assigned to any letter.\n- Reduce totals by summing digits, except master numbers 11 and 22 which are preserved and read as master vibrations with their reduced digit (11 → 2, 22 → 4) noted alongside.\n- Mulank (Psychic number) comes from the birth DAY only. Bhagyank (Destiny number) comes from the full date DD+MM+YYYY digit sum. Name number comes from the full spelling of the name used publicly.",
